{
  "comment": "Canonical list of every MailerLite field the site's forms write to, so the upsert can refuse a key MailerLite would silently drop. The first eight are MailerLite built-ins that every account ships with; the setup script finds them already present and leaves them alone, but its post-check then verifies the keys. MailerLite derives a field's key from its display name and splits runs of capitals (its own 'ZIP' became z_i_p), so display names here deliberately avoid all-caps words. MailerLite only supports the types text, number and date: every Yes/No answer is stored as the text 'Yes' or 'No', and multi-select answers as a comma-separated text list. Fields prefixed cope_ belong to the COPE GOTV volunteer form (/cope-gotv); the rest to the get-involved form (/). Run `npm run setup:mailerlite` to create any that don't exist yet.",
